<%
// Family Name filter select for a bulk-print member picker - a real
// request: "all bulk printing should have filter by family name."
// Reused across every member-based Design/Print panel (Schedule Cards,
// Name Tags, Name Tags + Schedule Cards front/back, Barcodes Only,
// Barcode Mailing Labels, Name Tag Requests) so an admin can narrow a
// picker's checkbox list down to one family before selecting/printing.
// Client-side filtered against each row's own data-family-id (views/
// partials/print-picker-table.ejs) by public/js/design-print-hub.js's
// wireBulkMemberList - the same mechanism the existing Type filter
// already uses on these same panels, not a page reload. That's
// deliberately different from the Members/Schedule page's own family
// filter (views/admin-schedule.ejs), which round-trips a real page
// reload - there the whole page (and its own server-side query) is
// scoped to one filter combination at a time; here every panel's full
// member list is already sitting in the DOM (see print-picker-table.ejs's
// own comment on why), so re-filtering it in the browser is both
// consistent with the Type filter beside it and avoids six separate
// reloads of the same member set. Locals: id (the <select>'s own unique
// DOM id - every panel needs its own), families (utils/members.js's
// allFamilies()).
%>
<select class="name-tag-bulk-filter-select" id="<%= id %>">
  <option value="">All Families</option>
  <% families.forEach(function(f) { %>
    <option value="<%= f.id %>"><%= f.name %> Family</option>
  <% }); %>
</select>
